  "summary": "A self-taught Software Engineer with 10+ years at Costco Wholesale. I began my career as a warehouse employee, spending 2.5 years on the floor before transitioning into the IT side of the business. During my time in the warehouse, I developed and refined skills that have translated strongly into the IT space. That foundation, combined with my natural curiosity and continuous pursuit of growth, has opened many doors—and continues to do so.\n\nCurrently working with IBM BAW (20.0.0.X, 19.0.0.X, 18.0.0.X) and IBM BPM 8.5.\n\nHands-on experience with:\n- IBM Business Process Diagram modeling and implementation\n- Teamworks (TW) Process Designer, including UCAs, SLAs, message events, timer events, intermediate and activity-level timers\n- IBM Cloud Toolchains and Code Engine for application deployment and automation\n- IBM Cloud App ID for authentication and access management\n- IBM ISV API integrations with BAW applications\n- Process Portal – Portal Customization, Custom Dashboards\n- Process Admin Console\n- Process Centre – Process Management, Snapshot, Deployment etc.\n\nOther Skills and Areas of Focus:\n- Technical Writing\n- Front-end Development, Web Development\n- JavaScript, ReactJS, Python\n- Containerization and Serverless\n- Network Engineering\n- Cloud Architecture",
